    "headline": "SA1 5-minute dispatch price peaked at $4,981.00/MWh for the interval ending 2026-07-31 02:05 ACST (UTC+0930).",
    "summary": [
      "In the investigated window the price ranged from $75.14/MWh to $4,981.00/MWh. The unweighted mean of the 5-minute prices was $416.71/MWh, and 214 five-minute intervals were at or above the project analysis threshold of $300.00/MWh (a project setting, not an AEMO label).",
      "At that interval, dispatch TOTALDEMAND (AEMO: 'Demand (less loads)', a dispatch quantity that is not operational demand) was 1,473 MW and NETINTERCHANGE ('Net interconnector flow from the regional reference node') was -83 MW.",
      "Actual operational demand (updated values) was 1,466 MW in the half-hour containing the price peak; the window maximum was 2,173 MW (half-hour ending 2026-07-30 19:00 ACST (UTC+0930)).",
      "The largest unit-level SCADA change in the 90-minute window starting one hour before the peak was AGLHAL (+49 MW); this is an observation, not an outage diagnosis.",
      "For the half-hours around the peak, the latest AEMO POE50 forecast available before each half-hour had a mean absolute error of 33 MW.",
      "Definitions used: [s03] \u201cTotal Demand is the forecast demand at the Regional Reference Node (RRN) that is met by local generation from scheduled and semi-scheduled generating units and scheduled BDUs plus interconnector imports, excluding the local demand of scheduled loads and scheduled BDUs and the allocated interconnector losses, but including the demand met by Wholesale Demand Response.\u201d [s04] \u201cRRP (NUMBER(15,5)): Regional Reference Price for this dispatch period.\u201d"
